IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`
IMPORT `cda-s10-interpretation`
IMPORT `cda-s5-lawful-excuse`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971, sections 1 to 3: THE OFFENCES.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Written from the text alone.
--
-- Each offence is a BOOLEAN over its elements, in the order the section states them:
-- the conduct, the circumstances, the state of mind, and "without lawful excuse"
-- (worked out by cda-s5-lawful-excuse.l4). The penalty is in cda-s4-punishment.l4:
-- these rules say whether an offence is committed, not what follows.
--
-- The Act defines none of "intending", "reckless" or "knows". They are facts the
-- person states (cda-nouns.l4); nothing here decides one for anybody.

§ `Section 1 -- Destroying or damaging property`

§§ `1(1) -- destroying or damaging property belonging to another`

-- src:5 | 1 Destroying or damaging property.
-- src:6 | (1) A person who without lawful excuse destroys or damages any property belonging to another intending to destroy or damage any such property or being reckless as to whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 1(1) (src:5-6)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` case MEANS
        -- "without lawful excuse". Section 5(1) applies to arson under 1(1) as to any
        -- other offence under 1(1), so the not-by-fire constructor stands for both.
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
        -- "destroys or damages"
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the damage`)
        -- "any property belonging to another"
    AND `property belonging to another` (case's `the property`)
        -- "intending to destroy or damage any such property or being reckless as to
        -- whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged"
    AND (   case's `intending to destroy or damage any such property`
         OR case's `reckless as to whether any such property would be destroyed or damaged`)

§§ `1(2) -- destroying or damaging property, intending or risking danger to life`

-- src:7 | (2) A person who without lawful excuse destroys or damages any property, whether belonging to himself or another—
-- src:8 | (a) intending to destroy or damage any property or being reckless as to whether any property would be destroyed or damaged; and
-- src:9 | (b) intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another or being reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered;
-- src:10 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 1(2) (src:7-10)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` case MEANS
        -- "without lawful excuse". Section 5 does not apply to 1(2) (s 5(1)), so only a
        -- lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2) is left.
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
        -- "destroys or damages any property, whether belonging to himself or another"
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the damage`)
    AND `a thing is property within section 10(1)` (case's `the property`'s `the thing`)
        -- (a) "intending to destroy or damage any property or being reckless as to
        -- whether any property would be destroyed or damaged"
    AND (   case's `intending to destroy or damage any property`
         OR case's `reckless as to whether any property would be destroyed or damaged`)
        -- (b) "intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another or
        -- being reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered"
    AND (   case's `intending by the destruction or damage to endanger the life of another`
         OR case's `reckless as to whether the life of another would be thereby endangered`)

§§ `1(3) -- arson`

-- src:11 | (3) An offence committed under this section by destroying or damaging property by fire shall be charged as arson.
@ref s 1(3) (src:11)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an offence under section 1 must be charged as arson` case MEANS
        (   `a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` case
         OR `a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` case)
    AND case's `the destruction or damage was by fire`

-- The offence under section 1(1), if one is committed, named as arson if by fire (s 1(3)).
@ref s 1(3) (src:11)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF Offence
`the section 1(1) offence committed, if any` case MEANS
    IF `a person commits an offence under section 1(1)` case
    THEN (IF case's `the destruction or damage was by fire`
          THEN LIST `arson under section 1(1)`
          ELSE LIST `an offence under section 1(1), not by fire`)
    ELSE EMPTY

@ref s 1(3) (src:11)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF Offence
`the section 1(2) offence committed, if any` case MEANS
    IF `a person commits an offence under section 1(2)` case
    THEN (IF case's `the destruction or damage was by fire`
          THEN LIST `arson under section 1(2)`
          ELSE LIST `an offence under section 1(2), not by fire`)
    ELSE EMPTY

-- Both can be committed by one act: the Act does not make them alternatives.
@ref s 1(3) (src:11)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 1 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF Offence
`the offences committed under section 1` case MEANS
    append (`the section 1(1) offence committed, if any` case)
           (`the section 1(2) offence committed, if any` case)

§ `Section 2 -- Threats to destroy or damage property`

-- src:12 | 2 Threats to destroy or damage property.
-- src:13 | A person who without lawful excuse makes to another a threat, intending that that other would fear it would be carried out,—
-- src:14 | (a) to destroy or damage any property belonging to that other or a third person; or
-- src:15 | (b) to destroy or damage his own property in a way which he knows is likely to endanger the life of that other or third person;
-- src:16 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 2 (src:12-16)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 2 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 2` case MEANS
        `a person commits an offence under section 2(a)` case
    OR  `a person commits an offence under section 2(b)` case

-- The elements common to (a) and (b): "makes to another a threat, intending that that
-- other would fear it would be carried out". The intention is about the fear, not
-- about carrying the threat out: nothing in section 2 requires the threat to be meant.
@ref s 2 (src:13)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 2 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the threat was made to another, intending that that other would fear it would be carried out` case MEANS
        case's `a threat made to another`
    AND case's `intending that that other would fear it would be carried out`

-- (a) "to destroy or damage any property belonging to that other or a third person".
-- "That other or a third person" is any person but the accused (see NOTES.md, fork F5).
@ref s 2(a) (src:14)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 2 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 2(a)` case MEANS
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 2(a)` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
    AND `the threat was made to another, intending that that other would fear it would be carried out` case
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the threatened damage`)
    AND `property belonging to another` (case's `the property threatened`)

-- (b) "to destroy or damage his own property in a way which he knows is likely to
-- endanger the life of that other or third person". Section 5 does not apply (s 5(1)).
@ref s 2(b) (src:15)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 2 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 2(b)` case MEANS
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 2(b)` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
    AND `the threat was made to another, intending that that other would fear it would be carried out` case
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the threatened damage`)
    AND `property belonging to the accused` (case's `the property threatened`)
    AND case's `knowing it likely that the threatened destruction or damage would endanger the life of that other or a third person`

§ `Section 3 -- Possessing anything with intent to destroy or damage property`

-- src:17 | 3 Possessing anything with intent to destroy or damage property.
-- src:18 | A person who has anything in his custody or under his control intending without lawful excuse to use it or cause or permit another to use it—
-- src:19 | (a) to destroy or damage any property belonging to some other person; or
-- src:20 | (b) to destroy or damage his own or the user’s property in a way which he knows is likely to endanger the life of some other person;
-- src:21 | shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 3 (src:17-21)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 3` case MEANS
        `a person commits an offence under section 3(a)` case
    OR  `a person commits an offence under section 3(b)` case

-- The elements common to (a) and (b): "has anything in his custody or under his
-- control intending ... to use it or cause or permit another to use it". Nothing in
-- section 3 requires the thing to be of any kind, or the use to be imminent or to happen.
@ref s 3 (src:18)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the accused has the thing intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it` case MEANS
        case's `anything in the accused's custody or under the accused's control`
    AND case's `intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it, to destroy or damage property`

-- (a) "to destroy or damage any property belonging to some other person".
@ref s 3(a) (src:19)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 3(a)` case MEANS
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 3(a)` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
    AND `the accused has the thing intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it` case
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the intended damage`)
    AND `property belonging to another` (case's `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged`)

-- (b) "to destroy or damage his own or the user's property in a way which he knows is
-- likely to endanger the life of some other person". Section 5 does not apply (s 5(1)).
@ref s 3(b) (src:20)
GIVEN case IS A `Section 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person commits an offence under section 3(b)` case MEANS
        (NOT (`the accused has a lawful excuse for` `an offence under section 3(b)` (case's `lawful excuse`)))
    AND `the accused has the thing intending to use it, or cause or permit another to use it` case
    AND `destruction or damage within the Act` (case's `the intended damage`)
    AND (   `property belonging to the accused` (case's `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged`)
         OR (    `a thing is property within section 10(1)` (case's `the property intended to be destroyed or damaged`'s `the thing`)
             AND `property belongs to a person with this connection under section 10(2) to (4)` (case's `the user's connection with the property`)))
    AND case's `knowing it likely that the destruction or damage would endanger the life of some other person`
